  "files": {
    "THREAT_MODEL.md": "# Threat model: file uploads\n\n## Assets\nUser files in uploads/, the host file system, other users' data.\n\n## Trust boundaries\nBrowser to service (untrusted filename, bytes and size), service to disk.\n\n## Threats\n- Path traversal: filename \"../../x\" writes outside uploads/ (save_upload joins it unchecked).\n- Overwrite of another user's file with the same name.\n- Oversized or many uploads exhausting disk.\n- Executable or HTML content served back to other users.\n\n## Mitigations\nGenerate server-side names, reject separators, enforce size and quota limits, store per user, serve with a download content type.\n"
  },
